<h2>The question</h2>

<p><a href="/backlog/3867-decision-should-a-delegated-vendor-graduate-past-spot-check/">#3867</a> asks whether a
delegated vendor (Codex, Gemini via Antigravity) that has a long, clean record at <code>spot-check</code> could
graduate one rung further — to a lighter level, or to no independent check at all. Rule 7 of
<a href="/docs/agent/platform-decisions/#delegation-trial-record-graduation">#delegation-trial-record-graduation</a>
(ratified via #3690) says the independent look "gets shallower but never goes away". This survey builds on
the #3690 survey, <a href="/research/delegation-graduation-and-supervision-tiers/">When has a delegated
non-Claude agent earned lighter supervision?</a>, and does not repeat it. The full working is in
<a href="/reports/2026-09-23-delegation-below-spot-check-grounding.md">the session report</a>.</p>

<h2>Finding 1 — spot-check is already at the floor</h2>

<p>The router has exactly two levels, <code>full</code> and <code>spot-check</code>
(<code>SUPERVISION_LEVELS</code> in <code>scripts/lib/provider-routing.mjs</code>). Rule 7 defines
<code>spot-check</code>'s independent pass by reference to
<a href="/docs/agent/platform-decisions/#every-pr-gets-a-look-advisory-floor">#every-pr-gets-a-look-advisory-floor</a>
(#3313): one tool-free juror, one round, the diff and the card, capped findings, non-blocking. #3313 gives
that floor to every PR that trips no escalation reason, whoever built it. So a graduated delegated triple is
already checked as lightly as ordinary Claude-built work.</p>

<p>Every reading of "lighter than spot-check" is already placed:</p>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Reading</th><th>Where it stands</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No independent pass</td><td>Rejected in #3690 Fork 5 (b), against #3313's "the capacity floor is never zero".</td></tr>
<tr><td>Review a sample of the triple's diffs</td><td>Rejected by #3313: "never a random sample of a few".</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rely on the PR's own review only</td><td>That is already what <code>spot-check</code> is.</td></tr>
<tr><td>A cheaper or batched juror</td><td>Not a level. It is the floor's own depth dial, changed for every PR, never per producer.</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>Finding 2 — removing the look breaks the loop that measures it</h2>

<p>A clean streak counts how often the independent pass found nothing. Remove the pass and no streak can
justify its removal. Three rules of the ratified model depend on it: a confirmed miss is a hard veto
(rule 3), the positive control is a trial where independent review found a real problem (rule 4), and
demotion is computed from the record (rule 6). With no independent look, misses stop arriving, positive
controls stop, and demotion can no longer fire. Promotion would become one-way.</p>

<p><strong>This breach already exists in code.</strong> <code>scripts/review-set-label.mjs</code> writes a
delegation trial row only while the triple is not yet graduated, and always as a clean
<code>landed</code> row. So once a triple graduates, its record stops growing and can never demote it.
The prep filed this as a separate build; it is owed whichever way #3867 is decided.</p>

<h2>Finding 3 — prior art keys lighter checking to the change, not the producer</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Depth moves, coverage stays:</strong> ANSI/ASQ Z1.4 / ISO 2859-1 reduced inspection samples
fewer items from every lot, and one rejected lot returns it to normal. Google requires an LGTM on every
change; readability waives only a co-signer.</li>
<li><strong>Coverage drops only as a sampler:</strong> ISO 2859-3 skip-lot lets whole lots through after
qualification, and one rejected lot ends it. This is the sampler shape #3313 already rejected.</li>
<li><strong>Per-item review is dropped by change class:</strong> Renovate and Dependabot automerge chosen
update types (lockfiles, dev dependencies, digests). Chromium's Rubber Stamper approves clean reverts,
clean cherry-picks and benign files, and "never provides OWNERS approval". SLSA lets an organisation give
a named "Trusted Robot" an exception — a governance act, not a streak.</li>
<li><strong>AI coding agents, Sept 2026:</strong> GitHub Copilot coding agent, OpenAI Codex, Devin and
Claude Code review all keep a required review before an agent PR merges.</li>
</ul>

<p>The WE delta: the proposal keys lighter checking to <em>who built it</em>; the prior art keys it to
<em>what kind of change it is</em>. The first breaks the measurement loop. The second does not, but it is a
builder-neutral change to #3313's floor, not to rule 7.</p>

<h2>What this survey does not settle</h2>

<p>Nothing here rules. The recommended verdict — no, keep rule 7 — and its re-open triggers are on
<a href="/backlog/3867-decision-should-a-delegated-vendor-graduate-past-spot-check/">#3867</a> itself.</p>
